@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "CRUD Operations";
}

<section>

    <!-- PAGE INTRODUCTION -->
    <div class="mb-5">

        <h1 class="fw-bold mb-3">
            CRUD Operations
        </h1>

        <p class="lead text-muted">
            CRUD stands for Create, Read, Update and Delete. These are
            the four basic operations performed on data stored in a
            database.
        </p>

        <p>
            Almost every database-driven application uses CRUD
            operations. In a Student Management System, for example,
            we can create a student record, read student information,
            update student details and delete a student record.
        </p>

    </div>


    <!-- WHAT IS CRUD -->
    <section class="mb-5">

        <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
            What is CRUD?
        </h2>

        <p>
            CRUD is a commonly used term in software development for
            describing the four fundamental operations performed on
            persistent data.
        </p>

        <div class="table-responsive">

            <table class="table table-bordered table-striped">

                <thead class="table-dark">

                    <tr>
                        <th>Operation</th>
                        <th>Meaning</th>
                        <th>Purpose</th>
                        <th>Common SQL Command</th>
                    </tr>

                </thead>

                <tbody>

                    <tr>

                        <td>
                            <strong>Create</strong>
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            Add new data
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            Creates a new record.
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            INSERT
                        </td>

                    </tr>

                    <tr>

                        <td>
                            <strong>Read</strong>
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            Retrieve data
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            Reads existing records.
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            SELECT
                        </td>

                    </tr>

                    <tr>

                        <td>
                            <strong>Update</strong>
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            Modify data
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            Changes an existing record.
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            UPDATE
                        </td>

                    </tr>

                    <tr>

                        <td>
                            <strong>Delete</strong>
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            Remove data
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            Deletes an existing record.
                        </td>

                        <td>
                            DELETE
                        </td>

                    </tr>

                </tbody>

            </table>

        </div>

    </section>


    <!-- CRUD DIAGRAM -->
    <section class="mb-5">

        <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
            CRUD Operations Flow
        </h2>

        <p>
            The four CRUD operations can be understood using the
            following flow:
        </p>

        <div class="code-block">

            <div class="code-lang-tag">
                CRUD
            </div>

            <pre class="mb-0"><code>
                    CRUD
                      |
        --------------------------------
        |              |              |
      CREATE          READ          UPDATE
        |              |              |
      INSERT         SELECT         UPDATE
        |
        -------------------------------
                      |
                    DELETE
                      |
                    DELETE
            </code></pre>

        </div>

    </section>


    <!-- CREATE -->
    <section class="mb-5">

        <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
            1. Create
        </h2>

        <p>
            The Create operation is used to add new records to a
            database table.
        </p>

        <p>
            In SQL Server, the <strong>INSERT</strong> statement is
            commonly used to perform the Create operation.
        </p>

        <div class="code-block">

            <div class="code-lang-tag">
                SQL
            </div>

            <pre class="mb-0"><code>INSERT INTO Students
(
    StudentId,
    StudentName,
    Age
)
VALUES
(
    101,
    'Rahul',
    22
);</code></pre>

        </div>

    </section>


    <!-- READ -->
    <section class="mb-5">

        <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
            2. Read
        </h2>

        <p>
            The Read operation is used to retrieve existing data from
            a database table.
        </p>

        <p>
            In SQL Server, the <strong>SELECT</strong> statement is
            used to read data.
        </p>

        <div class="code-block">

            <div class="code-lang-tag">
                SQL
            </div>

            <pre class="mb-0"><code>SELECT *
FROM Students;</code></pre>

        </div>

    </section>


    <!-- UPDATE -->
    <section class="mb-5">

        <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
            3. Update
        </h2>

        <p>
            The Update operation is used to modify existing data in
            a database table.
        </p>

        <p>
            In SQL Server, the <strong>UPDATE</strong> statement is
            used to modify existing records.
        </p>

        <div class="code-block">

            <div class="code-lang-tag">
                SQL
            </div>

            <pre class="mb-0"><code>UPDATE Students
SET Age = 23
WHERE StudentId = 101;</code></pre>

        </div>

    </section>


    <!-- DELETE -->
    <section class="mb-5">

        <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
            4. Delete
        </h2>

        <p>
            The Delete operation is used to remove existing records
            from a database table.
        </p>

        <p>
            In SQL Server, the <strong>DELETE</strong> statement is
            commonly used for this operation.
        </p>

        <div class="code-block">

            <div class="code-lang-tag">
                SQL
            </div>

            <pre class="mb-0"><code>DELETE FROM Students
WHERE StudentId = 101;</code></pre>

        </div>

    </section>


    <!-- REAL WORLD EXAMPLE -->
    <section class="mb-5">

        <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
            CRUD in Student Management System
        </h2>

        <p>
            Let's understand CRUD using a Student Management System.
        </p>

        <div class="table-responsive">

            <table class="table table-bordered table-striped">

                <thead class="table-dark">

                    <tr>
                        <th>Requirement</th>
                        <th>CRUD Operation</th>
                        <th>SQL Command</th>
                    </tr>

                </thead>

                <tbody>

                    <tr>
                        <td>Add a new student</td>
                        <td><strong>Create</strong></td>
                        <td>INSERT</td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td>Display student details</td>
                        <td><strong>Read</strong></td>
                        <td>SELECT</td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td>Change student details</td>
                        <td><strong>Update</strong></td>
                        <td>UPDATE</td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td>Remove a student</td>
                        <td><strong>Delete</strong></td>
                        <td>DELETE</td>
                    </tr>

                </tbody>

            </table>

        </div>

    </section>


    <!-- CRUD LIFECYCLE -->
    <section class="mb-5">

        <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
            CRUD Lifecycle
        </h2>

        <div class="code-block">

            <div class="code-lang-tag">
                CRUD
            </div>

            <pre class="mb-0"><code>
User
  |
  ↓
Create Data
  |
  ↓
Database
  |
  ↓
Read Data
  |
  ↓
Update Data
  |
  ↓
Delete Data
            </code></pre>

        </div>

    </section>


    <!-- CRUD AND SQL -->
    <section class="mb-5">

        <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
            CRUD and SQL Commands
        </h2>

        <div class="table-responsive">

            <table class="table table-bordered table-striped">

                <thead class="table-dark">

                    <tr>
                        <th>CRUD</th>
                        <th>SQL Command</th>
                        <th>Action</th>
                    </tr>

                </thead>

                <tbody>

                    <tr>
                        <td><strong>Create</strong></td>
                        <td>INSERT</td>
                        <td>Add record</td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td><strong>Read</strong></td>
                        <td>SELECT</td>
                        <td>Retrieve record</td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td><strong>Update</strong></td>
                        <td>UPDATE</td>
                        <td>Modify record</td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td><strong>Delete</strong></td>
                        <td>DELETE</td>
                        <td>Remove record</td>
                    </tr>

                </tbody>

            </table>

        </div>

    </section>


    <!-- IMPORTANT -->
    <section class="mb-5">

        <div class="alert alert-info border-0">

            <h5 class="fw-bold">
                Important
            </h5>

            <p class="mb-0">
                CRUD operations form the foundation of database-driven
                applications. In real-world applications, these
                operations are usually performed through application
                interfaces such as web pages, APIs or backend services.
            </p>

        </div>

    </section>


    <!-- SUMMARY -->
    <section class="mb-4">

        <div class="alert alert-primary border-0">

            <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
                Summary
            </h2>

            <p class="mb-0">
                CRUD stands for Create, Read, Update and Delete.
                Create uses INSERT to add data, Read uses SELECT to
                retrieve data, Update uses UPDATE to modify data and
                Delete uses DELETE to remove data. These four operations
                are fundamental to most database-driven applications.
            </p>

        </div>

    </section>


